            <ArticleTitle>The first nucleophilic C-H perfluoroalkylation of aromatic compounds via (arene)tricarbonylchromium complexes.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>2146-2149</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1039/c6cc09905j</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>The first nucleophilic perfluoroalkylation of arenes is based on the arene π-system activation via (η6-arene)tricarbonylchromium complexes. Perfluoroalkyl anions generated from Me3SiRF and a fluoride ion source [Me4N]F exclusively attack the arene ligand under mild conditions. The formed negatively charged analogs of Meisenheimer adducts readily undergo a one-pot oxidation to perfluoroalkyl arenes.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
